{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChFKVvJ12Lkzhoa2EXsqg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[x] A role string with a provider and the allowed flags parses to its provider, model, effort, max turns and prefer-subagent values; an unknown flag or an extra positional is rejected\n[x] `maxRounds` and `minRounds` default to 3 and 1; a value that is not a positive integer, or `minRounds` greater than `maxRounds`, is rejected\n[x] A missing `implement` or `review` inside `adversarial` is rejected\n[x] A `.redeye.json` that is not valid JSON makes the run exit 2 and creates no branch or worktree\n[x] An `adversarial` role string with an unsupported flag makes the run exit 2 and creates no branch or worktree\n[x] `--dry-run` with `adversarial` configured prints the implement and review role strings, `maxRounds` and `minRounds`\n[x] With no `.redeye.json`, or one without an `adversarial` key, a run behaves as it does today (existing integration tests stay green)\n\nThe ticket is done. Most of it was already on this branch from earlier commits (US-001, -002, -003 and -005), so I checked that each checklist item has a real, passing test instead of rewriting the code. The build and the full `npm test` run both pass, and lint is clean.\n\n**One bug fixed (commit `53731ed`).** An `adversarial` value that was not an object (a string, `null`, a number or an array) quietly turned the loop off. The spec says a value of the wrong shape should stop the run with exit 2. `loadConfig` in `src/config.ts` now throws in that case, and also when the whole file is valid JSON but not an object (for example `[]`). I wrote the tests in `test/config.test.ts` first and watched them fail before making the change. The README's `.redeye.json` section now lists this error too.\n\n**Test-runner gotcha.** In tapzero, `t.throws` is async. If the function doesn't throw, the failure is reported after a non-async test has already finished, so the run crashes with an error instead of printing `not ok`. The new tests are `async` and `await t.throws(...)`. I added a line about this to `AGENTS.md`.\n\n**Not touched:** `tsc --noEmit -p .` reports type errors in four test files (`display`, `integration`, `orchestrator` and `review`). They're outside this ticket, and they don't affect the build or `npm test`. My notes are in `.redeye/notes.md`, which is not committed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":171,"cache_read_input_tokens":73847,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":171},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b8712a23-7ba4-4c3f-bcaa-1036a452ea18","uuid":"bdef599e-05b8-43fb-afc3-a81d6627a942","timestamp":"2026-11-21T02:55:21.708Z","request_id":"req_011ChFKVv4cbr1h6tVxr15nD"}
